            <ArticleTitle>ACUTE HYDRONEPHROSIS MIMICKING RENAL COLIC.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>422-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Hydronephrosis may be acute, recurrent and related to ingestion of fluid. Frequently a lower polar vessel is an etiological factor. The condition is amenable to corrective operation by a variety of surgical techniques, as in the six cases here reported.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
